<!-- this is just a Doenet version of a WW exercise written by Chrissy Safranski -->

<setup>
  <function name="f">e^(-2*x)</function>
  <function name="fP">-2*e^(-2*x)</function>
  <function name="fPP">4*e^(-2*x)</function>
  <function name="fPPP">-8*e^(-2*x)</function>
  <function name="T3">$b0 + $b1*x + $b2*x^2 + $b3*x^3</function>
  <function name="T3P">$b1 + 2*$b2*x + 3*$b3*x^2</function>
  <function name="T3PP">2*$b2 + 6*$b3*x</function>
  <function name="T3PPP">6*$b3</function>
  <function name="T3Symb">b_0 + b_1*x + b_2*x^2 + b_3*x^3</function>
  <function name="T3PSymb">b_1 + 2*b_2*x + 3*b_3*x^2</function>
  <function name="T3PPSymb">2b_2 + 6*b_3*x</function>
  <function name="T3PPPSymb">6*b_3</function>

  <math name="a">0</math>
  <math name="b0">$$f($a)</math>
  <math name="b1">$$fP($a)</math>
  <math name="b2">$$fPP($a)/2</math>
  <math name="b3">$$fPPP($a)/6</math>
</setup>

<p>
  Let <m>f(x) = $f</m> and let <m>T_3(x) = b_0 + b_1x + b_2x^2 + b_3x^3</m>.  In what follows, we find the values of <m>b_0</m>, <m>b_1</m>, <m>b_2</m>, and <m>b_3</m> that make <m>$f</m> and <m>T_3(x)</m> have the same height, slope, concavity, and third derivative value at <m>x = 0</m>.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Complete the table below by computing derivatives of <m>f(x)</m> and <m>T_3(x)</m> and evaluating them at <m>x = 0</m> as directed.  Initially, several of your responses will involve the unknown coefficients <m>b_0</m>, <m>b_1</m>, <m>b_2</m>, and <m>b_3</m>.  Where needed, use underscores to enter the coefficients. For example, to enter <m>b_1</m> type <q>b_1</q>.

              <tabular>
                <row>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>f(x) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><m>$f</m></cell>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>T_3(x) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><m>b_0 + b_1x + b_2x^2 + b_3x^3</m></cell>
                </row>
               <row>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>f'(x) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="f1">$fP</answer></cell>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>T_3'(x) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="T21">$T3PSymb</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>f''(x) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="f2">$fPP</answer></cell>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>T_3''(x) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="T22">$T3PPSymb</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>f'''(x) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="f3">$fPPP</answer></cell>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>T_3'''(x) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="T23">$T3PPPSymb</answer></cell>
                </row>
              </tabular>

              <tabular>
                <row>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>f($a) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="fa">$$f($a)</answer></cell>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>T_3($a) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="T2a">$$T3Symb($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
               <row>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>f'($a) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="f1a">$$fP($a)</answer></cell>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>T_3'($a) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="T21a">$$T3PSymb($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>f''($a) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="f2a">$$fPP($a)</answer></cell>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>T_3''($a) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="T22a">$$T3PPSymb($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>f'''($a) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="f3a">$$fPPP($a)</answer></cell>
                  <cell halign="right"><m>T_3'''($a) = </m></cell>
                  <cell><answer name="T23a">$$T3PPPSymb($a)</answer></cell>
                </row>
              </tabular>      
      </p>    
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Now, since we want <m>T_3(x)</m> and <m>f(x)=$f</m> to have the same height at <m>x = $a</m>, we set <m>T_3($a) = f($a)</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        This implies <m>b_0 = </m><answer name="b0entered">$b0</answer>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Next, since we want <m>T_3(x)</m> and <m>f(x)=$f</m> to have the same slope at <m>x = $a</m>, we set <m>T_3'($a) = f'($a)</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        This implies <m>b_1 = </m><answer name="b1entered">$b1</answer>.
      </p>
      <p>
        In addition, since we want <m>T_3(x)</m> and <m>f(x)=$f</m> to have the same concavity at <m>x = $a</m>, we set <m>T_3''($a) = f''($a)</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        This implies <m>b_2 = </m><answer name="b2entered">$b2</answer>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Finally, since we want <m>T_3(x)</m> and <m>f(x)=$f</m> to have the same third derivative value at <m>x = $a</m>, we set <m>T_3'''($a) = f'''($a)</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        This implies <m>b_3 = </m><answer name="b3entered">$b3</answer>.
      </p>      
      <p>
        Putting everything together, the resulting formula for <m>T_3(x)</m> is 
      </p>
      <p>
        <m>T_3(x) = </m><answer name="T3Entered">$T3</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>